    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447-a3">

                <pb facs="0522" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 329.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stern to Mr. Jackson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hotel de Russie</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kissingen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: In answer to yours of the 2d,
                    received to-day, I beg to state that the U. S. commercial agent at Bamberg sent
                    me a copy of the letter he received from the Bavarian Government, and my lawyer
                    has been conferring with the authorities here, without any result, for the
                    reason that the retraction demanded by the gentleman was such that, considering
                    the wide publicity the affair has now reached, I could not conscientiously sign
                    the same.</p>
                <p>Will inform you of the result of the trial by telegraph Monday.</p>
                <p>Most respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Stern</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
